## Context

Child of tracker 0008 (split by raid f9e483: the ticket bundled five sign-off units over ~25 files). Read 0008's body and log for the up-front decisions: `Kind` is a `Literal`, `ACCEPTS` a `frozenset[str]`; one `DEFAULT_ORDER` constant for the cascade; no `detail_url` (no consumer found); contract as data plus a signature, no ABC/Protocol/base class.

Line endings: cli.py, config.py and sources crossref, hal, libgen, scihub, unpaywall, url are CRLF; keep each file's endings, no whole-file diffs.

## Actions
`from doifetch import Request, Result, fetch` as the stable import path; `doifetch.fetch(req)` runs the
default cascade (`DEFAULT_ORDER`). `import doifetch` has no side effects.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] Public library API: `from doifetch import Request, Result, fetch`; `doifetch.fetch(req)` runs the
      default source cascade, not one source
- [ ] `import doifetch` has no side effects and needs no extra: no network, no prompt (Firefox cookie,
      ISTEX), no optional dependency imported; a test imports it with the extras absent
